      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! Here is a draft for the \"Necessity of the Study\" section for your Horizon Europe grant proposal:\n\n---\n\n**Necessity of the Study**\n\nQuantum entanglement stands at the forefront of quantum physics, underpinning principles critical to the development of next-generation quantum technologies. Entanglement, a phenomenon where particles exhibit interconnected properties, despite spatial separation, is pivotal in enhancing quantum communication and computing. Our research at the University of Zurich aims to significantly advance the understanding of entanglement swapping, a process crucial for scalable quantum networks. Through rigorous experimentation and analysis, we intend to address existing conundrums in entanglement dynamics and decoherence—the loss of quantum coherence due to environmental interactions.\n\nAmidst the plethora of quantum research initiatives, our study emphasizes the synthesis of theories regarding the Bell inequality and the mechanics of non-locality, thereby reinforcing the fundamental aspects of quantum information theory. Our novel approach also targets the mitigation of decoherence in entanglement swapping, intending to bolster the reliability and efficiency of quantum computers. These contributions are instrumental in transitioning quantum science from theoretical abstractions to practical applications.\n\nA comprehensive investigation of these phenomena not only propels the understanding of quantum mechanics but also accelerates technological advancements in quantum computing and",
